---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy · AutoLog" description="What stays on your phone, and what leaves it.">
  <article class="reading-page reading-page--privacy">
    <header class="introduction">
      <p class="effective">Privacy · Effective 22 August 2026</p>
      <h1>Your drives<br />are personal.</h1>
      <p class="lede">What stays on your phone, and what leaves it.</p>
    </header>
    <section><h2>Where your data lives</h2><p>Trips, stats, and everything the app knows about your car are stored on your phone. There is no account, no sign-in, no analytics, and no AutoLog server. Delete the app and the data goes with it.</p></section>
    <section><h2>The two requests the app makes</h2><p>Both are best effort and silent. When they fail, the app skips them and moves on.</p></section>
    <section><h2>VIN decoding</h2><p>Your VIN is sent once to the NHTSA vPIC API, a US government service, to identify the car's make, model, and year. Nothing else is attached to the request.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Road geometry</h2><p>After a trip, the bounding box of the trip's area is sent to the Overpass API, an OpenStreetMap service, to fetch road shapes and names. The route you drove stays on the phone.</p></section>
    <section><h2>What the app never does</h2><p>It never uploads a route, never sells or shares driving data, and never scores your driving. There is no third party code in the app at all.</p></section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .introduction, section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .introduction { gap: 18px; }
  .effective { font-size: 14px; }
  h1 { font-size: 66px; line-height: 71px; }
  .lede, section p { line-height: 28px; }
  .lede { font-size: 18px; }
  section { gap: 14px; }
  h2 { font-size: 31px; line-height: 37px; }
  section p { font-size: 17px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    h1 { font-size: 43px; line-height: 48px; }
    h2 { font-size: 27px; line-height: 33px; }
  }
</style>
